$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\displaystyle\lim_{x\to 0}\dfrac{\tan(x)}{3x+\tan(x)}
\\\\
&=\displaystyle\lim_{x\to 0}\dfrac{\dfrac{d}{dx}[\tan(x)]}{\dfrac{d}{dx}[3x+\tan(x)]}\qquad\gray{\text{L’Hôpital’s rule}}
\\\\
&=\displaystyle\lim_{x\to 0}\dfrac{\sec^2(x)}{3+\sec^2(x)}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{\sec^2(0)}{3+\sec^2(0)}\qquad\gray{\text{Substitution}}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{1}{4}
\end{align}$

Note that we were only able to use L’Hôpital’s rule because the limit $\displaystyle\lim_{x\to 0}\dfrac{\dfrac{d}{dx}[\tan(x)]}{\dfrac{d}{dx}[3x+\tan(x)]}$ actually exists.
